AMD's revenue for FY2022 was $23.6 billion, up 44% from $16.4 billion in 2021. The change was driven primarily by:
- Data Center revenue, which rose 64% (largely from higher EPYC server processor sales);
- Gaming revenue, which increased ~21% (driven by higher semi‑custom product sales);
- Embedded revenue growth from the Xilinx embedded business;

partially offset by a ~10% decline in the Client segment due to weaker PC demand and significant inventory corrections in the second half of 2022.
